VIDEO 2 SCRIPT

Run Your Vercel Project Locally (Mac Setup)

Title:
Run Your Next.js App Locally (Mac Setup + Git)

⸻

0:00 – FULL FACE (Camera Large)

Say:

“In the last video, we deployed a Next.js app to Vercel.”

Pause.

“Now we’re bringing that same project to your own machine so you can actually start modifying it properly.”

Pause.

“This is Mac OS. It’s similar on Windows, but I’m demonstrating on Mac.”

Pause.

“Let’s make it real.”

Hard cut.

⸻

0:25 – FULL SCREEN SHARE

Open GitHub repository from Episode 1.

Say:

“This is the project Vercel created for us. Right now, it lives online.”

Pause.

“We’re going to copy it to our computer.”

⸻

0:50 – Install Node.js (Mac)

Open terminal.

Say:

“Before we run this locally, we need Node.js. Node lets your computer run JavaScript projects.”

Check if installed:

node -v

If not installed, say:

“If this doesn’t return a version number, install Node from nodejs.org.”

Open browser briefly.

Then return.

Keep it short.

⸻

1:40 – Clone Repository

Copy repo URL.

In terminal:

git clone <repo-url>
cd project-name

Say:

“Cloning just means copying the project to your machine.”

Pause.

⸻

2:10 – Install Dependencies

Run:

npm install

Say:

“This installs the project dependencies — basically everything this app needs in order to run.”

Let it finish.

No overtalking.

⸻

3:00 – Start Development Server

Run:

npm run dev

Say:

“This starts a local development server.”

Open browser to:

http://localhost:3000

Pause.

Say:

“This is now running on your own computer.”

Scroll slightly.

⸻

3:50 – Make a Local Change

Open project folder in code editor.

Change headline again to:

“Running Locally Now”

Save file.

Refresh browser.

Pause.

Say:

“And now it updates instantly.”

Short pause.

⸻

4:40 – Explain the Loop

Say:

“This is your local development loop.”

Pause.

“You edit locally. You test locally.”

Pause.

“When you’re ready, you push to GitHub.”

⸻

5:10 – Push Update

In terminal:

git add .
git commit -m "Update headline locally"
git push

Say:

“Now we push it back to GitHub.”

Switch to Vercel.

Show automatic redeploy.

Refresh live site.

Pause.

Say:

“And now production updates.”

⸻

6:10 – Authority Line

“Local development gives you control.”

Pause.

“Deployment is easy. Control is what makes you consistent.”

Keep it subtle.

No heavy philosophy.

⸻

6:40 – CTA

“If you’re serious about building this safely, start with The SaaS Starting Point. It will give you structure before you scale.”

Pause.

“I’ll see you in the next one.”

⸻

6:55 – Soft Preview

Stay on screen.

Say:

“In the next video, we’ll connect a real database to this project so it can actually store data.”

Pause.

“That’s when it starts becoming a real SaaS.”

End.

⸻

Important Notes

Keep it:
	•	Calm
	•	Direct
	•	No Git deep dive
	•	No terminal flexing
	•	No AI tools yet

AI workflow comes in Episode 3.